4-ab81-8d2dbfdc260c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285915} {:answer/id #uuid "9c4c2e56-1385-574b-8f8c-3a2929263137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "N" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286220} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d6502d-e765-57e5-a4ff-c4004b19e180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286774}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284954} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e91ea5-623a-5b06-99ad-8e38db33673c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287518}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "db5f24a8-6bb9-526d-89dd-0ad32386f5f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-181686" :question/problem "![](images/67/67eeabfcff4eb24e14c15691c1c9de746a8870808197739577f7696faeada5bc.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,4,\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,4x+1\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=4$ and *below* the line $y=4x+1.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<4,\\,y<4x+1.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=4$ and $y=4x+1$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1\\}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dd6acf5e-4f3a-5dae-82c6-2a7fc3e68a15" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433493}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433496 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287718 :question/answer-fields 